---
import SiteLayout from "@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Hero from "@/components/blocks/Hero.astro";
import Prose from "@/components/content/Prose.astro";
import Link from "@/components/ui/Link.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/lib/site";

/** Bump when the text changes. */
const updated = "29 October 2026";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site stores, what it measures and who handles it. No ads, no tracking cookies, no banner."
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="What this site knows about you"
    lead="Not much. There are no ads, no tracking cookies and nothing sold or shared for marketing. Here is everything it does."
  />

  <Prose class="privacy">
    <p class="text-caption privacy__updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <h2>Who runs it</h2>
    <p>
      I’m {SITE.name}, a Lead Product Designer, and this is my personal site. I’m responsible for
      any personal data it handles. If you have a question about it, write to me at{" "}
      <Link href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</Link>.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. To deliver pages and keep the site safe from abuse,
      Cloudflare processes technical data from every request, such as your IP address, browser and
      the page you asked for. I don’t see or keep those logs. You can read how Cloudflare handles
      them in its <Link href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</Link>.
    </p>

    <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
    <p>
      I use Cloudflare Web Analytics to see which pages people read and roughly where visits come
      from. It doesn’t use cookies, doesn’t store anything on your device and doesn’t follow you
      across sites. I only see totals: page views, referring sites, countries, browsers and device
      types. No individual visitor can be picked out.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      The site doesn’t need your consent for anything it stores, because each item is there only to
      do something you asked for or to keep the site running:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>case_study_access</strong> is a cookie set only after you enter the password for a
        protected case study, so you don’t have to type it again. It lasts 30 days and holds no
        personal data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>theme</strong> is saved in your browser’s local storage when you switch between
        light and dark mode, so the site remembers your choice.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>nav-collapse</strong> lives in session storage for a moment while the menu animates
        between pages, and is removed as soon as the next page loads.
      </li>
      <li>
        Cloudflare may set a security cookie such as <strong>__cf_bm</strong> or
        <strong>_cfuvid</strong> to tell people from bots.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      If you email me, I keep the conversation in my inbox so I can reply and follow up. I don’t add
      anyone to a mailing list.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you can ask me what I hold about you, and ask me to correct or delete it. Just
      email me. If you think I’ve handled your data badly, you can also complain to a data
      protection authority. In Poland that’s <Link href="https://uodo.gov.pl/en">UODO</Link>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  @layer components {
    .privacy {
      padding-block-end: var(--space-section-md);
    }

    .privacy__updated {
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
    }
  }
</style>
